Sean. go check on our reservation.

507
00:41:51.770 --> 00:41:53.570
They're gonna seat us right away.
Can't you wait after dinner.

508
00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:55.920
Might be closed by then!
Come on. SJ.

509
00:41:55.970 --> 00:41:58.530
- Please.
- I need some new magazines.

510
00:42:00.730 --> 00:42:03.100
Michael. come on. Come on.

511
00:42:13.710 --> 00:42:16.270
Collins! Collins!

512
00:42:17.530 --> 00:42:19.070
Collins. Come on!
Your dad's already PO'ed.

513
00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:21.750
- Lets' go. Come on.
- Over here.

514
00:42:23.150 --> 00:42:24.550
Mike.

515
00:42:29.840 --> 00:42:31.850
Remember this one. Mom?

516
00:42:31.900 --> 00:42:34.800
You read it to us
like thousand times.

517
00:42:34.940 --> 00:42:39.140
"And he gnashed his terrible teeth
and he roared his terrible roar."

518
00:42:39.750 --> 00:42:41.330
I always liked this one.

519
00:42:41.380 --> 00:42:43.960
Oh. Ferdinand...
Me too.

520
00:42:45.520 --> 00:42:49.570
Michael. your mama ever read
either one of those books to you?

521
00:42:52.200 --> 00:42:53.200
No?

522
00:42:54.530 --> 00:42:56.030
How cute.

523
00:42:56.370 --> 00:42:57.730
It was a good steak.

524
00:42:57.780 --> 00:43:00.510
- Thank you. Daddy.
- Thank you for lovely dinner. Papa.

525
00:43:00.560 --> 00:43:02.110
Here we go.

526
00:43:37.410 --> 00:43:38.830
Michael?...

527
00:43:38.880 --> 00:43:42.150
Who was that boy you were
talking to. at the restaurant?

528
00:43:42.200 --> 00:43:43.700
Marcus.

529
00:43:44.830 --> 00:43:47.260
Marcus. And he works there?

530
00:43:47.300 --> 00:43:48.800
Yeah.

531
00:43:50.030 --> 00:43:52.030
How do you know him?

532
00:43:53.430 --> 00:43:55.230
He's my brother.

533
00:44:02.130 --> 00:44:05.230
Well. we'd really like
to meet him someday.

534
00:44:06.310 --> 00:44:08.710
Would that be okay with you?

535
00:44:09.030 --> 00:44:11.430
I don't know where he stays.

536
00:44:11.600 --> 00:44:14.250
When's the last time you saw him?

537
00:44:17.010 --> 00:44:19.210
When I was little mebbe.

538
00:44:23.270 --> 00:44:29.510
"Once upon a time in Spain. there was a
little bull and his name was Ferdinand.

539
00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:34.280
All the other little bulls he lived with
would run and jump

540
00:44:34.330 --> 00:44:36.830
and butt their heads together.

541
00:44:37.930 --> 00:44:39.830
but not Ferdinand.

542
00:44:41.670 --> 00:44:46.020
He liked to sit just quietly
and smell the flowers.

543
00:44:48.450 --> 00:44:52.400
He had a favorite spot out in the pasture
under a cork tree.

544
00:44:53.920 --> 00:44:56.170
It was his favorite tree

545
00:44:56.220 --> 00:45:01.410
and he would sit in its shade all day
and smell the flowers."

546
00:45:01.950 --> 00:45:04.250
- Good night.
- Good night.

547
00:45:08.080 --> 00:45:09.570
What?

548
00:45:09.970 --> 00:45:11.970
Why are you smiling?

549
00:45:12.370 --> 00:45:16.010
I don't know. I'm just happy.
Really happy.

550
00:45:16.860 --> 00:45:19.890
Does this happiness have anything
to do with Michael?

551
00:45:19.940 --> 00:45:21.440
No.

552
00:45:22.510 --> 00:45:25.360
It has everything to do with Michael.

553
00:45:29.560 --> 00:45:31.210
Happy's good.

554
00:45:31.990 --> 00:45:34.130
You know what I think we should do?

555
00:45:34.180 --> 00:45:37.120
We should start a charity
for kids like Michael.

556
00:45:37.170 --> 00:45:37.910
Okay.

557
00:45:37.960 --> 00:45:40.500
- Maybe fund a program at Wingate.
- Sure.

558
00:45:40.550 --> 00:45:43.290
Lord knows that school
could use a little color.

559
00:45:43.340 --> 00:45:46.840
Michael's like a flying and milking
that place.

560
00:45:47.110 --> 00:45:49.310
Are you listening to me?

561
00:45:52.280 --> 00:45:59.570
I try to concentrate on one...
thing... at a time.

562
00:46:00.600 --> 00:46:03.780
You knew I was multi-tasker
when you married me. right?

563
00:46:03.830 --> 00:46:07.180
- I sure did.
- Alright. Okay. Let's check it.

564
00:46:11.560 --> 00:46:15.460
Okay. Tuohy family.
Big smiles everyone!

565
00:46:16.690 --> 00:46:20.090
And. one . two. three...

566
00:46:23.170 --> 00:46:26.540
Michael! Michael come over here
and get in the next one.

567
00:46:26.590 --> 00:46:29.780
Come on. Come on. Come over here.

568
00:46:35.090 --> 00:46:38.270
Oh. come on. It's not like I'm gonna
put it on the Christmas card.

569
00:46:38.320 --> 00:46:42.460
Okay. let's scootch in a little tighter.

570
00:46:42.650 --> 00:46:44.250
That's good.

571
00:46:45.040 --> 00:46:46.570
Really big smiles.

572
00:46:46.620 --> 00:46:50.230
Okay. one. two three... say Rebels!

573
00:46:50.330 --> 00:46:51.830
"Rebels"

574
00:46:55.150 --> 00:47:00.600
<i>TV commentary</i>

575
00:47:00.650 --> 00:47:02.150
I got it.

576
00:47:03.070 --> 00:47:05.520
- Who's winning?
- Tennessee.

577
00:47:06.130 --> 00:47:08.200
- Who are they playing?
- Clemson.

578
00:47:08.250 --> 00:47:10.740
Your mom roots against Tennessee
no matter who they're playing?

579
00:47:10.790 --> 00:47:13.590
Oh. yes. I do. With gusto.

580
00:47:13.680 --> 00:47:15.780
She can't stand Tennessee.

581
00:47:15.830 --> 00:47:19.040
Collie-bell. I thought you were
going to your boyfriend's?

582
00:47:19.090 --> 00:47:21.990
I thought of hanging around here today.

583
00:47:23.430 --> 00:47:25.030
I like that.

584
00:47:25.210 --> 00:47:28.050
Hey. baby. There's a coupla messages
on the machine but I didn't check 'em.

585
00:47:28.100 --> 00:47:29.600
Alright.

586
00:47:30.640 --> 00:47:34.170
<i>Hey. Sean. hey. Leigh Anne.
It's cousin Bobby. Happy New Years!</i>

587
00:47:34.220 --> 00:47:36.220
Listen. I've had about five cold ones...

588
00:47:36.270 --> 00:47:39.970
- Of course she had. - So I'm...
I'm just gonna go ahead and ask...

589
00:47:40.020 --> 00:47:43.370
Ya'll know there's a colored boy
in your Christmas Card?

590
00:47:46.420 --> 00:47:47.650
What?

591
00:47:48.620 --> 00:47:54.100
You just looked teeny-tiny next to him.
Right? Like Jessica Lange and King Kong.

592
00:47:55.250 --> 00:47:57.910
Hey. does Michael get the family discount
at Taco Bell?

593
00:47:57.960 --> 00:48:01.410
Because if he does Sean's gonna lose
a few stores.

594
00:48:01.710 --> 00:48:02.950
He's a great kid.

595
00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:06.300
Well. I say make it official
and just adopt him.

596
00:48:07.740 --> 00:48:09.140
He's gonna be eighteen
in a few months.

597
00:48:09.190 --> 00:48:12.540
Doesn't really make much sense
to legally adopt.

598
00:48:15.120 --> 00:48:18.980
Leigh Anne. is this some
sort of white guilt thing?

599
00:48:19.600 --> 00:48:21.850
What will your daddy say?

600
00:48:22.360 --> 00:48:25.810
Umm... before or after he turns over
in his grave?

601
00:48:25.980 --> 00:48:28.450
Daddy's been gone five years Elaine.

602
00:48:28.500 --> 00:48:30.790
make matters worse you were
at the funeral.

603
00:48:30.840 --> 00:48:34.260
Remember? You were Chanel
and that awful black hat.

604
00:48:34.310 --> 00:48:36.220
Look. here's the deal.

605
00:48:36.270 --> 00:48:39.320
I don't need y'all to approve
my choices. alright?

606
00:48:39.720 --> 00:48:42.130
But I do ask you to respect them.

607
00:48:42.180 --> 00:48:44.100
You've no idea what this boy's
been through.

608
00:48:44.150 --> 00:48:46.940
And If this is going to be
some running diatribe

609
00:48:46.990 --> 00:48:50.540
I can find an overpriced salad
a lot closer to home.

610
00:48:51.740 --> 00:48:53.550
Leigh Anne. I'm so sorry.
We didn't intend to---

611
00:48:53.600 --> 00:48:55.160
No. We didn't really.

612
00:48:55.210 --> 00:48:58.480
I think. what you're doing is so great.

613
00:48:58.690 --> 00:49:01.240
To open up your home... to him.

614
00:49:01.790 --> 00:49:04.740
Honey. you're changing that boy's life.

615
00:49:04.860 --> 00:49:06.010
No.

616
00:49:07.040 --> 00:49:08.990
He's changing mine.

617
00:49:10.140 --> 00:49:13.440
That's awesome for you.
but what about Collins?

618
00:49:14.390 --> 00:49:15.540
What about Collins?

619
00:49:15.590 --> 00:49:18.490
Aren't you worried. I mean.
even just a little?

620
00:49:18.590 --> 00:49:20.890
He's a boy. a large. black boy.

621
00:49:20.940 --> 00:49:23.390
sleeping under the same roof.

622
00:49:25.830 --> 00:49:27.480
Shame on you.

623
00:49:32.150 --> 00:49:33.850
I've got this.

624
00:49:35.870 --> 00:49:38.070
Be honest with me. okay?

625
00:49:39.500 --> 00:49:42.800
Is Michael being here making
you uncomfortable?

626
00:49:43.830 --> 00:49:47.100
They're stupid kids.
who cares what they say.

627
00:49:47.400 --> 00:49:48.690
What kids?

628
00:49:48.740 --> 00:49:50.110
At school.

629
00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:52.440
They're juvenile.

630
00:49:52.490 --> 00:49:55.240
And what do they juvenile kids say?

631
00:49:55.690 --> 00:49:58.290
It's really not worth repeating.

632
00:49:58.940 --> 00:50:02.720
And don't worry about SJ;
he likes all the attention.

633
00:50:03.320 --> 00:50:06.320
He introduces Michael
as his big brother.

634
00:50:10.170 --> 00:50:12.990
- What about you?
- It's fine.

635
00:50:15.710 --> 00:50:19.030
I mean. you can't just throw him
out on the street.

636
00:50:19.080 --> 00:50:21.580
I can make other arrangements.

637
00:50:25.150 --> 00:50:26.670
- Hi. Mike.
- Hi.

638
00:50:26.720 --> 00:50:28.720
- Need a push?
-Yeah.

639
00:50:35.200 --> 00:50:36.910
Higher. Mike! Higher!

640
00:50:40.780 --> 00:50:42.280
Higher!

641
00:50:47.230 --> 00:50:48.730
Higher!

642
00:50:52.960 --> 00:50:55.520
Don't look down.
Don't look down!

643
00:51:29.340 --> 00:51:31.740
- Where are you going?
- Collins?

644
00:51:43.910 --> 00:51:46.360
Quit looking at me like that.

645
00:51:46.410 --> 00:51:49.110
I mean. we study together at home.

646
00:52:05.960 --> 00:52:10.610
You know how much those things weigh?
This kid's gonna make us all famous.

647
00:52:12.080 --> 00:52:13.920
Easy. Bert. man.
It's only the spring

648
00:52:13.970 --> 00:52:16.400
he hasn't even been through
his first practice yet.

649
00:52:16.450 --> 00:52:18.250
No. He's a player.

650
00:52:21.150 --> 00:52:22.790
Ready.

651
00:52:23.500 --> 00:52:25.380
Get down. son.
Get down in your stands.

652
00:52:25.430 --> 00:52:26.970
In your stands!

653
00:52:27.590 --> 00:52:28.740
Go!

654
00:52:34.540 --> 00:52:36.140
Mike! Son!

655
00:52:36.880 --> 00:52:40.150
You fall off the block and then
you wanna shuck-shuck the blocker.

656
00:52:40.200 --> 00:52:43.090
Right? Shuck it!
Alright? Let's go!

657
00:52:46.090 --> 00:52:47.490
Papa?

658
00:52:48.770 --> 00:52:50.520
How's he doing?

659
00:52:50.690 --> 00:52:53.140
Doesn't quite have
the hang of it yet.

660
00:52:59.560 --> 00:53:01.260
Hey. Mike. Son...

661
00:53:01.540 --> 00:53:03.840
Shuck the blocker. Don't hold him!

662
00:53:07.250 --> 00:53:10.610
No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No.

663
00:53:21.870 --> 00:53:23.920
Balloons! There are balloons!

664
00:53:24.350 --> 00:53:27.200
Guys. quit looking at the balloons.
Everybody.

665
00:53:27.340 --> 00:53:30.460
Most kids from bad situations
can't wait to be violent

666
00:53:30.510 --> 00:53:32.320
and that comes out on the field.

667
00:53:32.370 --> 00:53:35.660
This kid. he acts like he doesn't want
to hit anyone.

668
00:53:35.710 --> 00:53:37.560
He's Ferdinand the Bull.

669
00:53:37.610 --> 00:53:39.690
- What?
- Nothing.

670
00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:42.550
I thought sure he was gonna be a player.

671
00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:45.590
I can't believe I used up my chiefs
to get him in school.

672
00:53:45.640 --> 00:53:48.890
I thought you said it was
your Christian duty?

673
00:53:49.530 --> 00:53:52.580
Look. Bert. He's never played before.

674
00:53:53.370 --> 00:53:56.910
And he won't this fall if he doesn't
improve a lot before then.

675
00:53:56.960 --> 00:53:59.090
Who xxx made him Bert bright?

676
00:53:59.870 --> 00:54:01.520
Unbelievable!

677
00:54:03.020 --> 00:54:04.870
Oh. God bless me.

678
00:54:05.360 --> 00:54:06.960
This is your summer workout sheet.

679
00:54:07.010 --> 00:54:10.160
Now. first it says to warm up
and get loose.

680
00:54:10.400 --> 00:54:12.400
Go ahead. get loose.

681
00:54:15.010 --> 00:54:16.310
Are you loose?

682
00:54:16.970 --> 00:54:20.770
Okay. next is five one hundred yard runs
to stretch out your legs.

683
00:54:20.820 --> 00:54:22.390
Let's go home.
play some video games.

684
00:54:22.440 --> 00:54:26.550
Look. everybody at Wingate is expecting
you to be a star football player.

685
00:54:26.600 --> 00:54:28.290
You don't want to let
them down. do you?

686
00:54:28.340 --> 00:54:29.080
Iono.

687
00:54:29.130 --> 00:54:30.430
What about Dad and Mom?

688
00:54:30.480 --> 00:54:33.410
'Cause you see. in our family
everyone's an athlete.

689
00:54:33.460 --> 00:54:35.120
Dad was a basketball star.

690
00:54:35.170 --> 00:54:37.470
Collins plays volleyball
and runs track.

691
00:54:37.520 --> 00:54:40.050
And me. as you know. I do it all.

692
00:54:40.100 --> 00:54:42.750
And Mom...
Mom was a cheerleader.

693
00:54:42.830 --> 00:54:45.950
which doesn't exactly count
but don't tell her I said that.

694
00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:47.350
- Okay?
- Okay.

695
00:54:47.400 --> 00:54:48.560
Okay.

696
00:54:51.290 --> 00:54:54.730
...fifty. fifty one.

697
00:54:56.020 --> 00:54:59.200
fifty two. fifty three...

698
00:54:59.250 --> 00:55:01.870
Come on and get it!
Go. go. go. go. go!

699
00:55:02.060 --> 00:55:04.690
Come on. Five seconds left in the game!

700
00:55:06.140 --> 00:55:08.460
Just like!
Just like!

701
00:55:08.660 --> 00:55:11.540
High knees. high knees. high knees!
xxx baby.

702
00:55:11.840 --> 00:55:13.340
Run like the wind!

703
00:55:14.880 --> 00:55:16.650
Go. Michael. go!

704
00:55:17.140 --> 00:55:20.090
...ninety eight. nine.

705
00:55:22.010 --> 00:55:23.210
one hundred.

706
00:55:23.260 --> 00:55:25.290
Move your feet! Move your feet!
Come on! Come on! Come on!

707
00:55:25.340 --> 00:55:27.190
Go. There you go.

708
00:55:27.350 --> 00:55:30.150
Get on the tackle!
Come on! Come on! Come on!

709
00:55:30.870 --> 00:55:32.720
Come on. Michael!

710
00:55:56.950 --> 00:55:58.050
Mrs. Tuohy?

711
00:55:58.100 --> 00:56:01.680
I hear "Mrs. Tuohy" I look over my
shoulder for my mother-in-law.

712
00:56:01.730 --> 00:56:05.180
Call me Leigh Anne or Mama
or almost anything else.

713
00:56:07.920 --> 00:56:10.920
- Can you help me get something?
- What?

714
00:56:13.260 --> 00:56:15.110
Driver's licence.

715
00:56:16.430 --> 00:56:20.680
Why do you need a driver's licence
when you don't even have a car?

716
00:56:27.150 --> 00:56:30.250
Michael. why do yo want
a driver's licence?

717
00:56:30.430 --> 00:56:33.400
Something to carry.
With my name on it.

718
00:56:40.260 --> 00:56:43.150
There's nobody named
Michael Oher in the system.

719
00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:45.500
Another last name perhaps?

720
00:56:47.880 --> 00:56:50.700
Look. I will sign something
that says he lives with us

721
00:56:50.750 --> 00:56:54.350
and we'll pay for all the insurence;
whatever it takes. okay?

722
00:56:54.860 --> 00:56:56.060
What's it gonna take?

723
00:56:56.110 --> 00:56:58.910
- You wanna do what?!
- You heard me.

724
00:56:59.080 --> 00:57:02.290
- Shouldn't we at least talk about this?
- What do you think we're doing?

725
00:57:02.340 --> 00:57:04.650
And don't act like I'm going
behind your back.

726
00:57:04.700 --> 00:57:08.430
I know you put us down as Michael's
medical contact at school.

727
00:57:08.480 --> 00:57:11.570
There's a huge difference between
paying for broken arm

728
00:57:11.620 --> 00:57:13.510
and being legally responsible
for someone.

729
00:57:13.560 --> 00:57:15.510
I mean the kid we barly know.

730
00:57:15.560 --> 00:57:18.850
That's another thing. We need
to find out more about his past.

731
00:57:18.900 --> 00:57:20.915
He won't talk about it.
He's like an onion.

732
00:57:20.965 --> 00:57:22.980
you have to peel him back
a layer at a time.

733
00:57:23.030 --> 00:57:25.180
Not if you use a knife.

734
00:57:26.160 --> 00:57:29.510
What if we took him to a child
psychologist or something?

735
00:57:29.560 --> 00:57:32.150
- Do you really expect Big Mike---
- "Michael"

736
00:57:32.200 --> 00:57:35.570
You really expect Michael to lie down
on a coach and talk about his childhood

737
00:57:35.620 --> 00:57:36.940
like he's Woody Allen or something?

738
00:57:36.990 --> 00:57:39.770
I mean. Michael's gift
is his ability to forget.

739
00:57:39.820 --> 00:57:44.270
He's mad at no one and he really
didn't care what happened in the past.

740
00:57:44.610 --> 00:57:46.260
You're right.

741
00:57:46.450 --> 00:57:47.950
Excuse me?

742
00:57:48.090 --> 00:57:49.660
"You're right?"

743
00:57:49.710 --> 00:57:52.350
How'd those words taste
coming out of your mouth?

744
00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:54.050
Like vinegar.

745
